<<<
rest, habit may be thought inferior to habitude; In the new land the fetters of habitude fall off./All the great habitudes of every species of animals have repeatedly been proved to be independent of imitation./They can be learned only by habitude & conversation. The sense
===
rest, *habit* may be thought inferior to *habitude*; *In the new land the fetters of habitude fall off./All the great habitudes of every species of animals have repeatedly been proved to be independent of imitation./They can be learned only by habitude & conversation.* The sense
>>>

